= Appendix I — Comparisons

== I.1 Structures and actions

*Ligament versus tendon:* ligament connects bone to bone; tendon connects muscle to bone.  
*Artery versus vein:* artery carries blood away from the heart; vein carries blood towards it. Oxygen content is not the defining distinction.  
*Flexion versus extension:* flexion decreases a joint angle; extension increases it.  
*Abduction versus adduction:* away from versus towards the midline.

== I.2 Fitness and participation

*Strength versus endurance:* force production versus sustaining or repeating effort.  
*Frequency versus intensity:* how often versus how hard.  
*Leisure versus recreation:* available free time versus an activity chosen for enjoyment or renewal.  
*Equality versus equity:* identical treatment versus attention to differing needs and barriers. Both concepts depend on context.

== I.3 Competition

*Round robin versus single knockout:* participants meet others according to the schedule versus elimination after a loss. Competition-specific rules may add extra rounds or tie-breaks.
